Answer to the question in the subject line of the article - No.

Pets promote to higher monster types based on experience
gained in combat.  Pets only engage in combat when they
are on the same level at you.  Abandon a pet, it's no longer
on the same level as you, it no longer participates in combat
(too hard to implement in the code, not worth estimating),
so it long longer gains hit points, so it no longer promotes to
a stronger monster type.

If you want your baby dragon to grow up to be an adult
dragon you need to keep it with you.  Or push it into a
polymorph trap and maybe get a grid bug, maybe get an
adult dragon ...


